        <briefdescription>
<para>Whether the console output uses colours. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Set by <computeroutput>--color[=&lt;when&gt;]</computeroutput>, as in the GNU tools, where <computeroutput>&lt;when&gt;</computeroutput> is <computeroutput>always</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>never</computeroutput>, or <computeroutput>auto</computeroutput>, or one of their GNU synonyms (<computeroutput>yes</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>force</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>no</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>none</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>tty</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>if-tty</computeroutput>), and <computeroutput>--color</computeroutput> alone means <computeroutput>always</computeroutput>; the value is accepted only after <computeroutput>=</computeroutput>. The alternative <computeroutput>--use-colour=&lt;mode&gt;</computeroutput> or <computeroutput>--use-colour &lt;mode&gt;</computeroutput>, as in Catch2 and Boost UT, takes <computeroutput>yes</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>no</computeroutput>, or <computeroutput>auto</computeroutput>, and also accepts the other values of <computeroutput>--color</computeroutput>. Used only by the human reporter.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="since"><para>5.1.0 </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
