      <memberdef kind="variable" id="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1runner__options_1a8dc9c5a5b6c89c12acd27d67d57618dd" prot="public" static="no" mutable="no">
        <type>std::vector&lt; std::string_view &gt;</type>
        <definition>std::vector&lt;std::string_view&gt; micro_os_plus::micro_test_plus::runner_options::filter_patterns</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>filter_patterns</name>
        <qualifiedname>micro_os_plus::micro_test_plus::runner_options::filter_patterns</qualifiedname>
        <initializer>{}</initializer>
        <briefdescription>
<para>The patterns that select the suites and the test cases to run, one per nesting level. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Each <computeroutput>--filter=&lt;pattern&gt;</computeroutput> or <computeroutput>--filter &lt;pattern&gt;</computeroutput> option adds one pattern; unlike the other options, <computeroutput>--filter</computeroutput> may be repeated. As with <computeroutput>--grep</computeroutput> in node-tap, the first pattern applies to the suite names, the second to the names of the test cases, and each further pattern to the names of the test cases nested one level deeper; the levels without a pattern are not filtered.</para>
<para>Within a pattern, <computeroutput>|</computeroutput> separates alternatives; a name matches when it matches any of them, as defined by <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-utility-functions_1gaa2f0f4cff320a783ad2347c9ff3fc731" kindref="member">utility::is_match()</ref></computeroutput>: <computeroutput>*</computeroutput> matches any sequence of characters, <computeroutput>?</computeroutput> matches any single character, the match is case-sensitive, and the alternative must cover the whole name.</para>
<para>The suites and the test cases that do not match are reported as skipped, and their bodies are not called. The top suite is never skipped as a whole, since its body is <computeroutput>main()</computeroutput>, but when its name does not match the first pattern, all its test cases are skipped.</para>
<para>When the list is empty (the default), everything runs.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="since"><para>5.1.0 </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
