      <memberdef kind="variable" id="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1runner__options_1ac4f95336439b329d0f3731a5dcafb6f9" prot="public" static="no" mutable="no">
        <type>bool</type>
        <definition>bool micro_os_plus::micro_test_plus::runner_options::list_tests</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>list_tests</name>
        <qualifiedname>micro_os_plus::micro_test_plus::runner_options::list_tests</qualifiedname>
        <initializer>{ false }</initializer>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Whether the test cases are listed instead of run. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Set by the <computeroutput>--list-tests</computeroutput> option, or by its short form <computeroutput>--list</computeroutput>. When set, the suite bodies run, as usual, to create their test cases, but the bodies of the test cases do not, so no check is evaluated. The selected test cases (see <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1runner__options_1a8dc9c5a5b6c89c12acd27d67d57618dd" kindref="member">filter_patterns</ref></computeroutput>) are listed under the names of their suites, as Catch2 lists them:</para>
<para><programlisting filename=".txt"><codeline><highlight class="normal">All<sp/>available<sp/>test<sp/>cases:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>Sample</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>Check<sp/>various<sp/>conditions</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>Check<sp/>strings</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>Explicit<sp/></highlight><highlight class="keyword">namespace<sp/></highlight><highlight class="normal">suite</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>Check<sp/>one</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">3<sp/>test<sp/>cases<sp/>in<sp/>2<sp/>test<sp/>suites</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para>The header is <computeroutput>Matching test cases:</computeroutput> when there are filter patterns, and the suites without selected test cases are not listed. The nested test cases are not listed, since they are created by the bodies of their parents, which do not run. The list is written to the console, unless the verbosity is <computeroutput>silent</computeroutput>, and to the output file, if any; no report is written, and <computeroutput>run()</computeroutput> returns 0, or 2 after an option error.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="since"><para>5.1.0 </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
