<para>Set by <computeroutput>--output-file=&lt;path&gt;</computeroutput> or <computeroutput>--output-file &lt;path&gt;</computeroutput>. When it is <computeroutput>nullptr</computeroutput> or empty, no file is written. The reporter opens the file, and keeps a copy of the path, when it is created by <computeroutput>initialise()</computeroutput>; if the file cannot be opened, the error is reported on <computeroutput>stderr</computeroutput>, the report is written only to the console, and <computeroutput><ref refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1runner_1a97f725cb167a2b464fac0eb88a0c8a46" kindref="member">runner::run()</ref></computeroutput> returns 2. </para>
