    <briefdescription>
<para>The configuration of a test session. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><computeroutput><ref refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1runner_1acfabd0e10d233ad305b6f4fc125a97f2" kindref="member">runner::initialise</ref> (argc, argv)</computeroutput> parses the command-line options into this structure and passes it to <computeroutput><ref refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1runner_1acfabd0e10d233ad305b6f4fc125a97f2" kindref="member">runner::initialise</ref> (options)</computeroutput>, which creates the selected reporter and starts the session.</para>
<para>The applications that do not have a command line, such as the embedded ones without semihosting arguments, can define the options directly, starting from the defaults, and call the second overload:</para>
<para><programlisting filename=".cpp"><codeline><highlight class="normal">mt::runner_options<sp/>options{};</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">options.selected_reporter<sp/>=<sp/>mt::reporter_kind::human;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">options.verbosity_level<sp/>=<sp/>mt::verbosity::verbose;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keyword">auto</highlight><highlight class="normal">&amp;<sp/>ts<sp/>=<sp/>tr.initialise<sp/>(options,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;Main&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">);</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para>The structure only refers to the strings it uses; they must remain valid until <computeroutput>initialise()</computeroutput> returns, which copies what it keeps.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="since"><para>5.1.0 </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
